# EBS Design System Rules

The approved EBS visual direction is:

Local-first
Modern
Friendly
Premium
Home-service oriented
Technology-enabled

Avoid:

- dark enterprise SaaS aesthetic
- neon AI styling
- cyberpunk visuals
- generic office stock photography
- excessive gradients
- excessive animation
- flashy AI-demo effects

Core brand colors:

--brand-navy: #143049
--brand-navy-deep: #0e2438
--brand-teal: #1EC8A5
--brand-teal-hover: #17B395
--brand-sky: #E6EEF4
--brand-warm: #F6F3EE
--brand-white: #FFFFFF
--brand-slate: #4F6274
--brand-forest: #4D6B5A

Brand atmosphere:

- warm off-white surfaces
- white cards
- navy typography
- teal CTAs
- soft sky-blue sections
- local homes
- neighborhoods
- mountains / foothills
- natural daylight

Photography should reinforce home-service/local-business context.

Aceternity-inspired interaction may be used sparingly.

Allowed:

- subtle Spotlight
- Hover Border Gradient
- Focus Cards
- mild viewport reveals
- subtle CTA arrow movement
- restrained topographic/elevation details

Avoid:

- Meteors
- Background Beams
- Vortex
- Lamp effects
- typewriter animations
- aggressive glow
- scroll hijacking

Priority order:

1. usability
2. customer clarity
3. local/home-service context
4. brand consistency
5. technical polish
6. decorative animation

All motion must respect prefers-reduced-motion.
